From 4ac4822249da0616c9b5f91107d44d63862c93b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:34:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hal: engine A's dialogue frames walk only the pixels that can
 draw

A dialogue box is one BG (BG3) inside WIN0 and ~2k composited pixels, but
the compose visited all 49k per pass. Same pictures:
- The BG loop goes layer by layer along each line (a pixel depends only on
  the layers before it at that pixel, so the paint order is unchanged),
  skips the columns the layer's window bit hides four at a time, and reads
  a tile's screen entry and row of texels once, passing a row with no
  opaque texel over whole. SM64DS_TWOD_VERIFY=1 against bg_loop_ref: 0
  mismatching composites.
- g_a_quiet: per row, which 8-column groups hold a hit (every writer marks
  its group through a_mark), so the clear and the final blit visit only
  those; the blit's brightness verdict reads the line's window mask once
  and a card-held cell is written by blit_ov_cell.
- hide_3d_outside_windows returns at once when every window region lets
  BG0 through (each dialogue box), bm_fill_default copies a row whose
  window rows match the last built row's without building it, and
  build_objwin clears its mask only after a window sprite wrote it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
